'' A WIDE CHAIN AS A SELECT CASE SUBJECT IS COMPARED WIDE. Check types '&' STRING, so
'' 'select case w & "y"' went to the narrow descriptor path, which has nothing to give for
'' a wide chain: the subject declined and the WHOLE SELECT was dropped, with no case run
'' and nothing said but "1 statements not lowered". Measured, fbc builds the chain with
'' fb_WstrConcatWA and compares each case value with fb_WstrCompare; it prints hit.
'' A family call over one -- 'right( "00" & wstr( 7 ), 2 )' -- is the same shape.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/select-wide-chain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrConcatWA(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrRight(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrCompare(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrDelete(
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrCompare(
